// Language codes and names.
//
// A character or a player's session can be pinned to one language. The SDK
// then tells Nur Live both the code (so the greeting, and anything said
// before the player's first words, come out in that language) and a name
// (the language the replies are held to). A regional code names the variety:
// `ar-EG` is Egyptian Arabic. Anything else is used as the name as written,
// so `languageName: "Kansai Japanese"` works for varieties not listed.

